  "pool": "paper",
  "stem": "The graph of the linear function \\(f\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane passes through the points \\((-3, 10)\\) and \\((5, -6)\\). If \\(f(k) = 0\\), what is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "2"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Slope: \\(\\frac{-6 - 10}{5 - (-3)} = \\frac{-16}{8} = -2\\).",
    "\\(f(x) = 10 - 2(x + 3) = -2x + 4\\).",
    "\\(-2k + 4 = 0\\), so \\(k = 2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nm = Rational(-6 - 10, 5 + 3)\nf = 10 + m*(x + 3)\nassert f.subs(x, 5) == -6\nsol = solve(f, x)\nassert sol == [2]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == sol",
